diff -ruN a/ROADMAP.md b/ROADMAP.md
--- a/ROADMAP.md	2026-10-16 23:31:22.569521819 +0000
+++ b/ROADMAP.md	2026-10-16 23:31:22.571314336 +0000
@@ -79,6 +79,12 @@
     - Trees: `Col` gained `leaf` / `lb` / `lmeta` / `ltint` / `log`; `column` reads through trunk and air to the ground; `build` draws the ground normally plus a leaf box (top, bottom, sides minus what the neighbouring crown hides) and a trunk at step 1; `resolve` keeps a forest cell's mass at the mean crown height (a quarter of the cell under leaves) and drops a lone tree. `TREES` 300 -> 520, `KEEP_TILES` 900 -> 700.
     - Cut: `indices` split into `covered` + `gather`; `Tile::cut` makes a new index buffer only when `covered` changed.
     - ponytail: no persistence; trunk only at step 1; edits far from the player only show once their chunk loaded; one worker; `TREES` 520 makes ~3x the generate + populate work of 300 (36 chunks per tile with its margin), first fill on a phone may take minutes (lower `TREES` if so). UNVERIFIED: that it compiles, speed and memory on a device, the look of the leaf boxes.
+- 2026-10-17: LoD rewritten as 3D voxels (Voxy `Mipper` / `RenderDataFactory`) - written WITHOUT a Rust toolchain: not compiled, not run. Tests first, with `--release`: `lod::tests::{a_column_is_runs_down_to_the_ground, a_mip_rounds_terrain_and_keeps_leaves, flat_ground_is_tops_only, a_tree_is_a_trunk_and_a_crown, the_cut_waits_for_the_real_mesh, a_tile_file_round_trips, an_ingested_chunk_replaces_the_guess, a_generated_tile_meshes, water_is_darker_the_deeper_it_is, pregen_goes_nearest_first_and_counts_chunks}`.
+    - Causes of the bugs seen in screenshots: (1) a column was ONE top block + ONE leaf box, so a tree was a box from the crown (or the ground) up and a mountain a pillar of its highest block; (2) the mip took the highest child of a footprint (terrain bloated by up to a step) at an arbitrary height; (3) the LoD was cut wherever the chunk ring was IN RANGE, even where the chunk had no mesh yet: a hole to the sky; (4) tiles not made yet were holes, and trees (slow) were asked before missing tiles.
+    - `world/lod.rs`: a column is runs of blocks (`Span`, top first, down to 4 blocks under the ground, stone below); a tile is meshed from a dense voxel grid (tile + 1 voxel margin from the neighbour tiles), mipped `log2(step)` times by `pick` (upper four children first, then solid > leaves > water, then Voxy's +y/+z/+x tie-break; solid when >= half of the children are, leaves/logs from one) and faced where a solid voxel meets a see-through one (`opaque`, water culls, same block culls). Water = one sheet on the top water voxel at 1/9 under its top, coloured by depth over its floor. Snow layer = 1/8 block at step 1, full block from step 2. Tile edge faces hang a skirt into the ground (neighbour at another step). Tile files are `L3` (old `L2` files are ignored and made again).
+    - `ChunkManager::drawn(k)` (chunk has a mesh) gates the cut; `Lod::update(.., gen = chunks.mesh_gen, drawn, in_frustum)` redoes the cut when `mesh_gen` changes. Missing tiles are asked first (bare, fast), trees second.
+    - Kept: `Lod::ingest`, pregen, `columns()` (now `Vec<Vec<Span>>`), fog, `RADIUS`, `step_for`. KEEP_TILES 700 -> 600 (a tile is ~100 KB, about 510 are in view).
+    - ponytail / not done: no greedy meshing (a step-1 forest tile is many quads), plants skipped, no water sides, no caves under the ground depth, no light (sky 15 everywhere), trees only within `TREES`. UNVERIFIED: the half-of-children rule and the distances are picked on paper; if distant terrain looks eroded raise it to "any child" for ids other than leaves (`pick`'s `need`), if bloated lower it.
 - 2026-10-16: MERGE of `Repo.zip` (Voxel LoD, Voxy style) and `Repo-merged.zip` (Tectonic, Nether, title screen, light thread, lazy noise, height-column distant terrain). Written WITHOUT a Rust toolchain: not compiled, not run. The common base was recovered by reversing `voxel-lod.patch` on `Repo.zip`; a three-way merge then left only the two LoD systems in conflict (`lib.rs`, README, ROADMAP); `mesh.rs` and `chunks.rs` merged cleanly.
     - Both replaced the same smooth heightfield LoD. The Voxel LoD is the one `App` draws: `App.lod: Option<Lod>` (was `far`), made by `new_lod` wherever the chunk manager is made (`reset_world`, `enter`; `Lod::new(self.seed, self.tectonic)`), none in the Nether, dropped by `quit_to_title`, drawn where `far` was, `camera.zfar = lod::ZFAR` (256 without it), fog ends at `lod::RADIUS`. `take_unloaded` is still drained and dropped (the Voxel LoD does not ingest real chunks; no persistence, so `far`'s `<world>/far` save call is gone).
     - Kept, not wired: the `lod/` crate and `world/far.rs` (`chunks.rs` still fills `unloaded` with `far::columns`, `camera.rs` still takes its initial `zfar` from `far::FAR_BLOCKS`). To go back to them: restore the `far` field, `new_far`, the `save` / `draw` / `update` calls and the fog line from the Repo-merged.zip `lib.rs`. UNVERIFIED: that `world/lod.rs` compiles against the merged generator (`OverworldGenerator::{new, tectonic, generate, populate}`, `WorldChunkManager::new`, `Region::new` are unchanged by the merged patches), run `cargo test -p tectonic -p embeddium -p lod` and `cargo test --lib --release` first.
